-- Regression test for lexical section scoping — FIX D, function-shaped
-- rebindings (spec §12).
--
-- The FIX D fixtures section-scoping-descendant-rebind.l4 and
-- section-scoping-sibling-later.l4 rebind ZERO-arity names, whose type is a
-- bare inference variable until the definition is inferred. A function-shaped
-- definition with a GIVEN but no GIVETH — the common L4 style — instead has
-- type FUNCTION FROM NUMBER TO <not yet inferred>, and one with no signature
-- at all has both ends open. Either shape, defined in a section BELOW the
-- reference, used to make the ancestor's own reference to the function
-- ambiguous:
--
--     There are multiple definitions for the identifier f
--
-- while the same rebinding placed ABOVE the reference resolved. The rule now
-- is that a not-yet-inferred off-ancestry candidate is DEFERRED: it is only
-- consulted when the ancestry does not already resolve the reference.

-- 1. GIVEN, no GIVETH; rebound in a child section below the reference.
§ a
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
f n MEANS n PLUS 1
g MEANS f 1                   -- 2: a's f, although §§ b rebinds f below

§§ b
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
f n MEANS n PLUS 2

-- 2. No signature at all; rebound in a child section below the reference.
§ c
h n MEANS n PLUS 10
k MEANS h 1                   -- 11: c's h, although §§ d rebinds h below

§§ d
h n MEANS n PLUS 20

-- 3. Two SIBLING sections, GIVEN only; each references its own.
§ `Title`
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
p n MEANS n PLUS 100
q MEANS p 1                   -- 101: Title's p, although `One` rebinds p below

§ `One`
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
p n MEANS n PLUS 200
r MEANS p 1                   -- 201: One's own p (same section first)

#EVAL a.g          -- 2
#EVAL c.k          -- 11
#EVAL Title.q      -- 101
#EVAL One.r        -- 201
